From dd9a525e869987764b7b553a828dbab4e2f6f7f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris <meischris39@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:39:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] USB: emulate an EyeToy on USB port 1

EyeToy games need a USB camera, and this core's USB was a stub that
answered every register with zero, so they had nothing to talk to.

Bring in the OHCI host controller from libretro/ps2 (its libretro-usb
directory, changed only for this tree's include paths and logging) and
PCSX2's EyeToy device model, which also covers the Konami Capture Eye.
The device is made by a plain factory instead of PCSX2's DeviceProxy and
has no microphone, so its audio endpoint returns empty packets. Pictures
come from the first V4L2 camera; with none, the game gets PCSX2's test
pattern once and nothing after it. The imported files keep their own
licence headers.

A new core option, System: USB Camera, plugs either camera into USB
port 1. The controller and its device live from USBinit to USBshutdown,
so suspending emulation does not unplug them, and the IRQ handler now
reports the interrupt as taken.

libjpeg is now required on Linux, for the camera's JPEG mode. USB state
is not in savestates yet.
